                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nandakumar B",
                        "email": "nandakumarb@ami.com",
                        "username": "Nandakumar-AMI"
                    },
                    "message": "These same new steps have also been added in:\nFile: ipmi/test_ipmi_payload.robot  \nKeyword: Verify Payload Version  \nCommit: (https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc-test-automation/+/88806)\n\nI suggest creating a common keyword called \"Verify the Channel Via IPMI\" and adding it to /lib/ipmi_client.robot.\n\nThis way, it can be reused from both ipmi/test_ipmi_general.robot and ipmi/test_ipmi_payload.robot"
                },
                {
                    "file": "ipmi/test_ipmi_general.robot",
                    "line": 396,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "zhengguowei",
                        "email": "zhengguowei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "zhengguowei12"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the suggestion.\n\nThe channel validation logic has been refactored into a common keyword **\"Verify the Channel Via IPMI\"** and moved to `/lib/ipmi_client.robot`.\n\nIt is now reused in `ipmi/test_ipmi_general.robot`,`ipmi/test_ipmi_payload.robot` and `ipmi/test_ipmi_cipher.robot` which helps reduce duplication and keeps the implementation consistent."
                }
